### 13. Test access request
POST /api/auth/access-requests

### 14. Access request, no token (expect 201, PENDING)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/access-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Sam",
  "last_name": "Rivera",
  "home_address": "5 Request Rd",
  "birth_date": "1999-05-05",
  "email_address": "sam.rivera@example.com"
}

### 15. Approve (expect 200 + username) - replace 5 with the id from the request above
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/auth/access-requests/3/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Login as the new user - use the username from the approve response
### and the temporary password printed in the app console email
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "srivera1006",
  "password": "PASTE_TEMP_PASSWORD_HERE"
}

### Send email as admin - replace 5 with the new user's id
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/3/send-email
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Account Notice",
  "body": "Your account has been reviewed."
}